This dossier supports first-time, never-licensed applicants preparing for the regular passenger-car written knowledge and road sign tests in Michigan. The issuing authority is the Michigan Department of State, led by the Secretary of State, and the source is the handbook What Every Driver Must Know. This section covers keeping right and its exceptions on ordinary roads and freeways, illegal weaving and median crossing, turn signals and hand signals, right and left turn technique including multiple turn lanes, changing lanes, roundabouts from approach to exit, and the opening railroad crossing rules. The handbook pages do not state an official question count, passing score, test format or time limit for the Secretary of State knowledge test, so this dossier asserts no value for any of them and records each as an explicit unknown. Practice scoring follows only the accepted LearningLoop product policy, never an official threshold.
